<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Ekim Yurtsever
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Center for Automotive Research</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="id8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Ohio State University
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Columbus, USA 
<br class="ltx_break">yurtsever.2@osu.edu
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Keith A. Redmill
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Electrical and Computer Engineering</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="id10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Ohio State University
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Columbus, USA 
<br class="ltx_break">redmill.1@osu.edu
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Autonomous driving in dense, dynamic environments requires decision-making systems that can exploit both spatial structure and long-horizon temporal dependencies while remaining robust to uncertainty. This work presents a novel framework that integrates multi-channel bird’s-eye-view occupancy grids with transformer-based sequence modeling for tactical driving in complex roundabout scenarios. To address the imbalance between frequent low-risk states and rare safety-critical decisions, we propose the Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer (UWDT). UWDT employs a frozen teacher transformer to estimate per-token predictive entropy, which is then used as a weight in the student model’s loss function. This mechanism amplifies learning from uncertain, high-impact states while maintaining stability across common low-risk transitions. Experiments in a roundabout simulator, across varying traffic densities, show that UWDT consistently outperforms other baselines in terms of reward, collision rate, and behavioral stability. The results demonstrate that uncertainty-aware, spatial-temporal transformers can deliver safer and more efficient decision-making for autonomous driving in complex traffic environments.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Occupancy Grids, Decision Transformer, Complex Driving Scenarios

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Autonomous driving is widely regarded as a key technology for improving road safety, reducing congestion, and increasing transportation efficiency. Achieving these benefits requires decision-making systems that can function reliably in dynamic, multi-agent environments such as intersections and roundabouts. In such settings, vehicles must perceive complex surroundings, anticipate interactive behaviors, and plan maneuvers that remain safe, efficient, and compliant with traffic rules even under uncertainty <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Common approaches to handle autonomous driving decision-making can be broadly categorized into modular rule-based planners, imitation learning, search-based methods, and reinforcement learning (RL). Modular planners decompose the driving task into perception, prediction, behavior planning, and control modules, enabling interpretability but requiring extensive manual design and tuning by subject experts. Imitation learning, particularly behavior cloning, learns policies directly from expert demonstrations but suffers from covariate shift and a dependence on large, diverse datasets. Search-based planners, such as Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS), generate interpretable maneuvers by simulating and evaluating candidate action sequences, yet their computational cost scales poorly with traffic density, limiting real-time applicability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. RL methods offer the potential to learn adaptive strategies through interaction, but online RL involves unsafe exploration, and many studies focus on simplified scenarios with limited generalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Decision Transformers (DTs) have recently emerged as a promising approach for offline reinforcement learning, reframing decision-making as a conditional sequence modeling problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. DTs leverage transformer architectures to capture long-horizon temporal dependencies without requiring unsafe online exploration. However, standard DTs are prone to performance degradation when encountering out-of-distribution states, often overfitting to frequent low-risk patterns while under-representing rare but safety-critical situations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. In other domains, reweighting strategies based on predictive uncertainty are widely used, such as focal loss, entropy-based knowledge distillation, and uncertainty-aware RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>. These methods have proven effective in mitigating imbalance and improving robustness.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Motivated by these insights, we propose the Uncertainty-weighted Decision Transformer (UWDT), a novel offline RL framework that combines multi-channel bird’s-eye-view occupancy grids for spatial representation with uncertainty-aware training (Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV Proposed method ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). A frozen teacher DT provides per-token predictive entropy, which is used to reweight the student DT’s loss, emphasizing rare, high-uncertainty states critical for safety. Our main contributions are:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An uncertainty-weighted training scheme that adaptively amplifies learning signals from safety-critical scenarios without altering the model architecture.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A comprehensive evaluation in a high-fidelity roundabout simulation across varying traffic densities, showing that UWDT outperforms baseline methods in reward, collision rate, and behavioral stability.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The paper is organized as follows. Section <a href="#S2" title="II Scenario Settings ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> defines the complex driving scenario. Section <a href="#S3" title="III Problem Formulation ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> introduces the reinforcement learning formulation for driving. Section <a href="#S4" title="IV Proposed method ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a> presents our proposed method, and Section <a href="#S5" title="V Results ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">V</span></a> provides the experimental results and analysis. Finally, Section <a href="#S6" title="VI conclusion ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI</span></a> concludes the paper and discusses future research directions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scenario Settings</span></h2>

<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.13132v1/figures/roundabout.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/398;" width="476" height="398" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>A four-arm, two-lane roundabout is used in our experiments.
The <span id="S2.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">ego vehicle</span> enters from the south, <span id="S2.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">circulating traffic</span> is already inside the roundabout and travels behind interacting traffic, <span id="S2.F1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008080;">interacting traffic</span> travels immediately ahead and behind the ego, and <span id="S2.F1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">exiting traffic</span> leaves from the east arm.
The dashed red polygon denotes the interaction zone, representing the ideal spatial region where traffic vehicles may interfere with or constrain the ego vehicle’s entry into the roundabout.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experimental setup, shown in Figure 
<a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II Scenario Settings ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the planner’s mission is to guide the ego vehicle entering the four arm, two lane roundabout from the south arm safely and efficiently to its fixed exit at the north arm, while negotiating circulating, interacting, and exiting traffic.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Initial states and randomness</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The initial lateral and longitudinal positions for background vehicles are described below. For every background vehicle, the initial speed</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(16,\,0.1^{2}\bigr)\,m/s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn> 0.1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\sim\mathcal{N}\bigl(16,\,0.1^{2}\bigr)\,m/s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is sampled independently and a Gaussian perturbation (<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\!=\!1\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\!=\!1\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math>) is added to each longitudinal position. Each vehicle perturbs the parameters of its Intelligent Driver Model (IDM) controller to introduce variation in acceleration and time-gap preferences.
These stochastic elements ensure that every episode presents the ego vehicle with a unique configuration of circulating, interacting, and exiting traffic.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Vehicle categories</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Traffic is divided into four functional groups that correspond to Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II Scenario Settings ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ego vehicle</span> (red).
Spawned <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="125\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>125</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">125\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math> before the south entrance on the inbound lane with an initial speed of 8 m/s.
Its fixed goal is the exit at the north arm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Circulating traffic</span> (orange).
A random number of vehicles</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{circ}}\sim\mathcal{U}\{0,1,2\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>circ</mtext></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{circ}}\sim\mathcal{U}\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">are initialized on the western approach and enter the roundabout, occupying either the inner or outer circulating lane.
Each vehicle selects a random destination among the north, east, or west exits, simulating diverse circulation behaviors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interacting traffic</span> (teal).
A random number of exiting vehicles</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{interact}}\sim\mathcal{U}\{0,1,2,3,4\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>interact</mtext></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{interact}}\sim\mathcal{U}\{0,1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">are inserted at varying positions along the circulating lanes.
These vehicles are likely to interfere with the ego vehicle’s entry decision, as they may block or yield at the merging point.
Their initial longitudinal offsets and lane assignments are randomized to reflect realistic variability in traffic flow.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exiting traffic</span> (blue).
Two vehicles are placed on the eastern approach, each at a distance of <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math> upstream from the roundabout.
They proceed directly toward the eastern exit, simulating through-traffic that does not engage with the ego vehicle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By increasing the number of interacting vehicles <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{interact}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>interact</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{interact}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we systematically escalate planning difficulty: higher <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{interact}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>interact</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{interact}}</annotation></semantics></math> values reduce available gaps, raise uncertainty in gap acceptance, and force the planner to negotiate tighter merge windows or defer entry behaviors, all of which dramatically elevate roundabout entry complexity under uncertainty. This design allows us to exploit rising MCTS computational costs, decision latency, and predictive entropy as a quantitative metric for scenario complexity, attributable to higher interacting vehicle counts.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation</span></h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reinforcement Learning for Driving Decision-Making</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The driving decision-making problem for vehicles in high-speed environments can be modeled as a Markov Decision Process (MDP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{P},r,\gamma)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{P},r,\gamma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state space; <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the action space; <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the state transition model; <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\xrightarrow{}\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\xrightarrow{}\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a reward function and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a discount factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Space.</span>
We adopt the default observation from <span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">highway‑env</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, a <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 41\times 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>41</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 41\times 50</annotation></semantics></math> Occupancy grid <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>.
The four channels correspond to <span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">presence</span>, longitudinal velocity <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, lateral velocity <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a binary <span id="S3.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">on_road</span> indicator.
The grid is centered on the ego vehicle, spans <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100\,\text{m}\times 82\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>82</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\,\text{m}\times 82\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and is discretised at <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\,\text{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\,\text{m}</annotation></semantics></math> resolution. All features are clipped to predefined ranges and linearly scaled to <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure numerical stability and compatibility with the CNN encoder used by our policy. This compact tensor representation preserves both spatial layout and dynamic context, enabling efficient convolutional processing of surrounding traffic interactions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Space.</span>
At each decision step <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> the policy selects one action <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> from</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{\text{llc},\ \text{rlc},\ \text{acc},\ \text{dec},\ \text{cruise}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>llc</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>rlc</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>acc</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>dec</mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>cruise</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{\text{llc},\ \text{rlc},\ \text{acc},\ \text{dec},\ \text{cruise}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">llc</span> stands for left lane change; <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text">rlc</span> stands for right lane change; <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.3" class="ltx_text">acc</span> stands for acceleration; <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.4" class="ltx_text">dec</span> stands for deceleration; <span id="S3.SS1.p3.2.5" class="ltx_text">cruise</span> stands for maintain speed.
This high-level action is then translated by a low-level motion planner into continuous control signals <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{acc},\theta_{lat})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{acc},\theta_{lat})</annotation></semantics></math> for acceleration and steering, where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{acc}\in[-1,1]\mathrm{m/s^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{acc}\in[-1,1]\mathrm{m/s^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{lat}\in[-\frac{\pi}{36},\ \frac{\pi}{36}]\,\mathrm{rad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>rad</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{lat}\in[-\frac{\pi}{36},\ \frac{\pi}{36}]\,\mathrm{rad}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function.</span>
Following the reward structures adopted in recent tactical-driving studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, the objective of the roundabout driving task encourages fast and safe driving while discouraging unnecessary lane changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Three scalar reward components are derived as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collision indicator <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the ego-vehicle has crashed and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The speed reward indicator <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the ego-vehicle’s speed is within the range <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[8,16]~\text{m/s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[8,16]~\text{m/s}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lane-change indicator <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when the chosen action commands a lane change, and <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The raw reward at each time step combines these components linearly with fixed weights from the default configuration:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{\text{raw}}=w_{c}c_{t}+w_{v}v_{t}+w_{\ell}\ell_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{\text{raw}}=w_{c}c_{t}+w_{v}v_{t}+w_{\ell}\ell_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where the collision weight <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{c}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{c}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> imposes a severe penalty upon collisions, the speed weight <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{v}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{v}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> provides a modest reward for maintaining high velocities (favoring efficient traffic flow without reckless acceleration), and the lane-change weight <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}=-0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}=-0.05</annotation></semantics></math> penalizes unnecessary lateral movements to encourage stable driving patterns. The reward is linearly scaled to <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}=\frac{r_{t}^{\text{raw}}-(w_{c}+w_{\ell})}{w_{v}-(w_{c}+w_{\ell})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}=\frac{r_{t}^{\text{raw}}-(w_{c}+w_{\ell})}{w_{v}-(w_{c}+w_{\ell})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">such that <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math> at collision and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math> when driving at the maximum speed without lane changes. This ensures a consistent reward range for training across episodes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Training Dataset</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To construct a high-quality offline training dataset, we employ MCTS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to generate 5,400 expert roundabout roll-outs. By leveraging the reward function, the trajectories generated by MCTS are well aligned with the downstream RL objective. Compared with heuristic or human-driven demonstrations, this procedure yields near-optimal yet unbiased expert trajectories that provide consistent and high-quality supervision for our DT and Transformer based behavior cloning baselines.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Proposed method</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce UWDT, an offline Decision Transformer framework designed to improve robustness in rare and safety-critical traffic scenarios by reweighting the training objective. UWDT proceeds in three stages:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.13132v1/figures/HDT.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/373;" width="476" height="373" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Teacher DT predictive uncertainty is estimated via the entropy of the action distribution. This entropy then acts as a weighting signal during student DT training, modulating the impact of each action prediction on the loss. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Teacher fitting:</span> train <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> on offline data and freeze its parameters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy extraction:</span> run <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> over the dataset to compute per-token entropies <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and normalize them into weights.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Student distillation:</span> optimize <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> with a weighted cross-entropy, allocating more gradient to high-entropy tokens.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This procedure requires no architectural changes and unifies uncertainty-aware distillation with offline-RL weighting. By up-weighting uncertain, safety-critical states while preserving temporal context, UWDT improves robustness to rare driving scenarios.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use a CNN encoder structure to capture spatial information. Each state tensor <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is encoded by a convolutional network:
three <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> convolutions with stride <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> (channels <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4\!\to\!32\!\to\!64\!\to\!128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\!\to\!32\!\to\!64\!\to\!128</annotation></semantics></math>),
ReLU activations, batch normalization, and spatial dropout.
The final feature map is flattened and projected to a fixed <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>–dimensional embedding <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}=\phi(s_{t})\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}},d_{e}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}=\phi(s_{t})\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}},d_{e}=32</annotation></semantics></math> via a lazy fully connected layer.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Teacher Decision Transformer</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt a standard DT as the teacher model. Given an offline dataset
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{\tau_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{\tau_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> of trajectories <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(s_{1},a_{1},r_{1},\dots,s_{T},a_{T},r_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(s_{1},a_{1},r_{1},\dots,s_{T},a_{T},r_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the return-to-go at time <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}=\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{\,k-t}\,r_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}=\sum_{k=t}^{T}\gamma^{\,k-t}\,r_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with discount <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
At each step <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the input token context is the interleaved sequence</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{1:t}=\bigl(R_{t},\,s_{t},\,a_{t-1},\,R_{t-1},\,s_{t-1},\,a_{t-2},\,\dots\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1:t}=\bigl(R_{t},\,s_{t},\,a_{t-1},\,R_{t-1},\,s_{t-1},\,a_{t-2},\,\dots\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A causal Transformer <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{T}(\cdot\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{T}(\cdot\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> is trained to predict the next action using input tokens.
Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the index set of valid tokens in a mini-batch and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the Teacher action distribution by <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{T,t}(a)=\pi_{T}(a\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{T,t}(a)=\pi_{T}(a\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The teacher loss is</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{T}(\theta_{T})=-\frac{1}{M}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\log p_{T,t}(a_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{T}(\theta_{T})=-\frac{1}{M}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\log p_{T,t}(a_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Gradient updates are performed with AdamW and a running‑mean‑square layer‑norm, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At test time, the next action is selected either by stochastic sampling or a greedy approach:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}=\begin{cases}\mathrm{sample}\!\bigl(p_{T,t}(\cdot)\bigr),&amp;\text{stochastic rollout},\\[4.0pt]
\displaystyle\arg\max_{a}\,p_{T,t}(a),&amp;\text{greedy rollout}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.992em;" width="2.992em"><mi>sample</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>stochastic rollout</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>a</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>greedy rollout</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}=\begin{cases}\mathrm{sample}\!\bigl(p_{T,t}(\cdot)\bigr),&amp;\text{stochastic rollout},\\[4.0pt]
\displaystyle\arg\max_{a}\,p_{T,t}(a),&amp;\text{greedy rollout}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In our experiments we adopt greedy rollout for stability and performance.
After convergence, <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is frozen and reused to compute per-token uncertainty for student training. Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ IV-A Teacher Decision Transformer ‣ IV Proposed method ‣ An Uncertainty-Weighted Decision Transformer for Navigation in Dense, Complex Driving Scenarios" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> lists the training parameters for the baseline DT and UWDT.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Symbol</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Meaning</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Value</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Context length (seq. window)</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">20</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Embedding dimension</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">32</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Discount factor for returns‑to‑go</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.99</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Learning rate</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Batch size</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">16</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Training epochs</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{wd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>wd</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{wd}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Weight decay (AdamW)</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\text{wu}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mtext>wu</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\text{wu}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Linear warm‑up ratio</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.1</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Gradient‑norm clip</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.25</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{layer}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{layer}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Transformer decoder layers</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">4</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b"><math id="S4.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{head}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{head}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">Attention heads</td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">1</td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Backbone DT hyper‑parameters</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Student Decision Transformer</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The student policy <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> shares the architecture with the Teacher DT. After obtaining the trained Teacher DT, we estimate predictive uncertainty by computing the entropy of its action distribution. During student training, this entropy serves as an uncertainty-based weight <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, modulating the loss contribution of each training token. Compared to the Teacher DT, the student is architecturally identical but trained with entropy-weighted supervision.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the student action distribution by
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{S,t}(a)=\pi_{S}(a\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{S,t}(a)=\pi_{S}(a\mid X_{1:t};\theta_{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each valid token we compute the masked cross-entropy scaled by <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{S}=-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\bar{w}_{t}\,\log p_{S,t}(a_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{S}=-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\bar{w}_{t}\,\log p_{S,t}(a_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Tokens with higher Teacher entropy carry larger gradient weight, encouraging the student to allocate additional capacity to states the Teacher found ambiguous. The Teacher’s predictive entropy is</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{t}=-\sum_{a=0}^{A-1}p_{T,t}(a)\log p_{T,t}(a),\qquad 0\leq H_{t}\leq\log A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}=-\sum_{a=0}^{A-1}p_{T,t}(a)\log p_{T,t}(a),\qquad 0\leq H_{t}\leq\log A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{T,t}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{T,t}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is the frozen Teacher action distribution and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of discrete actions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> denote the desired ratio between the largest and smallest per-token weights. We adopt a power mapping</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}_{t}=H_{t}^{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}_{t}=H_{t}^{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which increases its weight monotonically with entropy, so tokens where the teacher is less certain (larger <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) receive larger weights.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> UWDT training </figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
              
             Frozen <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\min},H_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\min},H_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leftarrow\dfrac{\ln r}{\ln(H_{\max}/H_{\min})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leftarrow\dfrac{\ln r}{\ln(H_{\max}/H_{\min})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{epoch}=1,\dots,E_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>epoch</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{epoch}=1,\dots,E_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              Sample mini-batch <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; build <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math>; get <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\leftarrow|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\leftarrow|\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}|</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for all</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{T,t}(a)\leftarrow\pi_{T}(a\mid X_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{T,t}(a)\leftarrow\pi_{T}(a\mid X_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{t}\leftarrow-\sum_{a}p_{T,t}(a)\log p_{T,t}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}\leftarrow-\sum_{a}p_{T,t}(a)\log p_{T,t}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{w}_{t}\leftarrow H_{t}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}_{t}\leftarrow H_{t}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\leftarrow\dfrac{1}{M}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\tilde{w}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\leftarrow\dfrac{1}{M}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}}\tilde{w}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for all</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{B}_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\leftarrow\tilde{w}_{t}/\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\leftarrow\tilde{w}_{t}/\mu</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{t}\leftarrow\min\{w_{t},\,w_{\max}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{t}\leftarrow\min\{w_{t},\,w_{\max}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
